      "side": 1,
      "message": "Steps to reproduce issue:\nNothing connect to pd port in S0 -\u003e apshutdown -\u003e connect dongle with AC and VGA in G3 (VGA connect to a monitor) -\u003e power button power on -\u003e DP doesn\u0027t output\n\nEC logs was posted in tracker #22 \"fail.txt\". I found that after we recieve DP config Ack and set usb mux USB_PD_MUX_USB_ENABLE and USB_PD_MUX_DP_ENABLE, then the hook function pd_chipset_startup() will be called and set the PD_EVENT_POWER_STATE_CHANGE event. finally in handle_new_power_state(), we get only USB_PD_MUX_USB_ENABLE mode and set it to mux. So DP is disabled and there isn\u0027t DP output.\n\nI think it needs a condition to check if the mux was configured or not, if yes, then we keep the setting; if not, then we can init it. But about this if condition, I\u0027m not sure it\u0027s appropriate or not.",
